// The Feud — Ali the Mayor after the Menaphite Leader is gone (§19.3). New file.
// CANDIDATE 2007-base (OSRS Transcript:The Feud §19.3 Talking to Ali the Mayor,
// minus the 27 Apr 2022 lore pass). World NPC multi feud_mayor 1869 @
// 3360,2970 L0 (m52_46 0 32 26); vis face feud_mayor_geom 1870 "Ali the
// Mayor" op1=Talk-to while %feud_mayor_invis 0 (multinpc=0,feud_mayor_geom —
// bind the vis name, not the multi base). Stand 3361,2970 E. Not on the NPC.
// Gate: %feud_var_menaboss >= 1 (Tough Guy killed, §18.5 PASS feudtsy35b22 —
// Leader gone, menaboss flag) else return. §19.3 verbatim, chat only. No
// stage write / no 28 / no dest / p_tele. No && / ||. The early
// welcome-to-Pollnivneach tree (§2.2) is NOT written.
// §21.5 Finishing up (Bandit champion dead, §20.4 PASS d478d3333):
// %feud_var_banditboss >= 1 dispatches @feud_mayor_nephew BEFORE the
// celebrate — "My thanks, adventurer. Your methods and motives may be
// questionable, but none can argue that you have delivered our little town
// from the wicked gangs who plagued it. I think things will change around
// here, now" / "that our problems are at a manageable size." / the nephew
// story ("greatest salesman", "a little too good", "angered the Menaphites
// and the bandits") / "smuggled him out" / "treasure trove" /
// "wholeheartedly apologise" / player "I think I may be able to help with
// one other thing... Ali the Operator." / "Now, how would a passing
// adventurer know where to find my missing jewels?" / "Er, let's just put
// it down to adventurer's intuition." Chat only, then return. No var writes.
// Cite copy-agent-opener-377.md · anchors-pollniv.md · feud-config-unit-first-377.md.

[opnpc1,feud_mayor_geom]
if (%feud_var_banditboss >= 1) {
    @feud_mayor_nephew;
}
if (%feud_var_menaboss < 1) { return; }
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>I don't know what we did to deserve your presence here, but I for one am filled with regret.");
~chatplayer("<p,angry>Well that's some show of gratitude! Can't I even get a 'thank you' for ridding your town of one of the gangs?");
~chatnpc("<p,quiz>Do you understand the concept of consequences?");
~chatplayer("<p,quiz>Er, I think so?");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Well, the consequences of your little piece of butchery are that the town is now even worse off. The bandits no longer have to waste time and energy fighting with the Menaphites and can direct all their attention");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>towards making us miserable. So for your efforts I thank you, but I wish no-one had asked for your help.");
~chatplayer("<p,neutral>I'll set this town right before I leave, I promise.");
~chatnpc("<p,shock>Why do I wish that you hadn't said that? Your heavyhanded tactics scare me.");
return;

[label,feud_mayor_nephew]
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>My thanks, adventurer. Your methods and motives may be questionable, but none can argue that you have delivered our little town from the wicked gangs who plagued it. I think things will change around here, now");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>that our problems are at a manageable size.");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>The least that I can do for you is answer your questions about the whereabouts of Ali Morrisane's nephew. He always was a mischievous young man, full of harebrained schemes.");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>He dreamed of being the greatest salesman in all of Gielinor! Unfortunately, he was a little too good.");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>He angered a number of people by coercing them into buying things they didn't really want. Completely within the law, of course, but the law could only protect young Ali for so long.");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Once he angered the Menaphites and the bandits, I knew I could no longer protect him.");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Under cover of darkness I smuggled him out of the town, and he's been gone ever since.");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>I can assure you, however, that he is safe and well - and now that you have effectively ended the threat posed by the gangs, he can continue his business elsewhere. Last I heard he planned to open some kind");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>of trade network with forty of his friends. A 'treasure trove', he claims. I'll believe it when I see it.");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>I hope that helps you in your quest. If you speak to Ali Morrisane, do tell him that I wholeheartedly apologise for the way he - er, his family - has been treated.");
~chatplayer("<p,neutral>I think I may be able to help with one other thing. I heard that your house was burgled recently. If you're interested in recovering the goods, you ought to have a word with Ali the Operator.");
~chatnpc("<p,quiz>Now, how would a passing adventurer know where to find my missing jewels?");
~chatplayer("<p,neutral>Er, let's just put it down to adventurer's intuition.");
return;
